**Binary DFA disposition:** drop production byte `plan`, `MAGIC/ABI`, BFS numbering/serialization, Python wire parser/LRU, `GrammarBatch` node uploads and poison-node ABI. No identified v3 consumer needs them: 2.3 uses factored tables plus runtime context. Retain the public concept `plan(actors, order_limit, hire_limit)` as the typed validated plan above. Its masks/cursor drive native validation and tests; Task 1.5's codec uses this source of truth through bindings. Replace binary-size/edge-offset tests with exhaustive reachable-state support/transition tests, deterministic tables, STOP reachability and the same state bound. The **reference** binary remains a fixture-generation oracle only. Record this clarification jointly with Claude because v4 still says “native plans”/`(node, slot)` (`W:docs/kaggriculture-contract.md:212–213`; H:29,43; `R:engine_rs/src/myolie_sampler.rs:268–325,493–535`).

