- [ ] Coupled-Gumbel enumeration's sequential law calls Rust grammar, every queue mass agrees, full 241/10 programs use length252, malformed inputs fail without narrowing/index faults.
- [ ] 320 accepted source-bound oracle programs (at least 200 required), with explicit real/synthetic and dense/full-market counts; negatives preserve both reference verdicts; fixture hashes and deterministic rerun checked.
- [ ] Decoded programs feed `Game::step`; executable-effect and replay-state comparisons prevent a vacuous acceptance-only result; dense 241-actor execution, the 240 → 241 HIRE capacity case and actor order pass (R3, R4).
- [ ] Strict `encode` round-trips every accepted program and replay action and rejects each listed malformed/over-capacity case with its category (R1).
- [ ] `grammar.rs` is self-contained and passes both packages' Clippy; the retirement condition for the engine-test include is recorded for 1.3/1.4 (R2).
